abstract: >-
  rgmin finds a local minimum of a smooth function from its value and
  gradient. It is built for geometry optimization. There, a host program
  such as eOn owns the loop, and a Solver takes one step per call. The
  step can stay on a manifold, such as the unit sphere or Cartesians with
  the rigid-body motions removed.
